    "created_at": "2016-06-21T12:46:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-21T12:46:10Z",
    "body": "I guess my mental model is that we have a handle on an object and on a method/property name. That is enough to be able to do a look up of the algorithm we want to run. Then we generate a origin-appropriate property descriptor that runs that algorithm.\n",
